# Reconciled Design System law (post-audit)

**Single source of truth:** Bricks Design Tokens **v1.2.0** in `design-system/tokens/`  
**Audit evidence:** `design-system-audit.md` (forensic pass over selected web PDP frames)  
**Proposed additions only (not law until approved):** `design-system/tokens-proposed-v1.2.1/`

The JSON is law. Frames were evidence. Do **not** invent a parallel system from frame raw values. Do **not** silently “fix” near-matches — if audit lists Near/Missing, ask before changing tokens or UI.

## Before any new UI (code or Figma)

1. Find an existing token in `design-system/tokens/` (or `--ds-*` / Bricks library binding).
2. Use / bind that token.
3. Only if nothing fits → stop and ask. Never introduce a raw hex/px/font because it matched a frame by eye.

## Auto-layout is mandatory

- Build every frame/group/component with auto-layout (`VERTICAL` / `HORIZONTAL`) by default.
- Capture real gap, per-side padding, alignment, hug/fill/fixed — never fake layout with absolute `x`/`y`.
- Absolute / `layoutMode: NONE` stacking is an **exception** only when the existing design explicitly used it (see audit). Do not invent new absolute layouts.

## Foundations to pull from JSON (not raw frame numbers)

| Need | Token files |
|---|---|
| Color | `color_primitives.*.json`, `color_tokens.*.json` |
| Spacing / gap / padding | `spacing.Value.tokens.json` |
| Radius | `radius.Value.tokens.json` |
| Type primitives | `typography.value.tokens.json` |
| Text styles | `text.styles.tokens.json` + Bricks library text styles when available |

Figma: bind **Bricks Design System** library variables/styles. Never create new variables or text styles unless the user explicitly extends the DS.

**Icons:** fetch only from [Iconography — Bricks](https://www.figma.com/design/Rq1j8iqvbJBYRb52tdpgFg/Iconography--Bricks-?node-id=7484-1322) (file key `Rq1j8iqvbJBYRb52tdpgFg`). See `bricks-iconography-source`. Never invent icon vectors.

## Platform

- Audited surfaces are **web**. Do not invent mobile spacing/type by guessing.
- Core identity (palette, radius scale, type family/weights, spacing steps) applies across platforms; web-specific page chrome stays web until a mobile audit exists.

## Proposed v1.2.1

`tokens-proposed-v1.2.1` may contain `audit_*` additive spacing/radius proposals from Missing findings. **Not approved by default.** Prefer v1.2.0 until the user accepts proposals via the audit.
